<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad Yar Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1902">1902</a>–<a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad Yar Khan was the last ruling Khan of Kalat, from 1933 to 1955. At the end of British rule in 1947 he declared Kalat independent, but in March 1948 he acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. He then headed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Baluchistan</a> States Union as Khan-e-Azam until it was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a> in 1955, and he later became governor of Balochistan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmad-yar-khan.jpg" alt="Ahmad Yar Khan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Toomanyyearskodakblack / AnonymousUnknown author (original) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JinnahBalochGov.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
